"""Editorial question designs for water systems and forest ecology."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


WATER = """history_origins|How a Water Source Changed|Which natural and human changes shaped one river, lake, or aquifer?|Compare dated flow, land-use, extraction, and community records.
famous_examples|A Water Project's Full Record|Did one celebrated water intervention improve quantity, quality, or access?|Compare baseline, measured outcomes, maintenance, and affected users.
hidden_stories|Who Keeps Water Flowing?|Whose monitoring, repair, and collection labor is absent from supply stories?|Use service records and attributed worker and household accounts.
beginner_explainers|Where the Water Goes|How does water move through one local catchment?|Map rain, runoff, infiltration, storage, use, and return flows.
advanced_concepts|Flow Is Not Supply|Why can high annual rainfall coexist with seasonal water scarcity?|Compare timing, storage, recharge, demand, and quality.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Did a Well Decline?|Which causes fit falling levels at one monitored well?|Compare pumping, recharge, nearby wells, seasonality, and measurement error.
technology_innovation|A Sensor in the Watershed|Did new monitoring improve decisions or just data volume?|Compare calibration, coverage, maintenance, and response outcomes.
people_personalities|Who Decides Water Allocation?|Which users and authorities shaped one allocation decision?|Trace rights, evidence, consultation, and unequal effects.
major_events|A Flood in the Record|Which conditions produced a documented flood and its impacts?|Compare rainfall, antecedent soil, land use, defenses, and exposure.
how_it_works|From Source to Tap|Which steps make raw water usable in one public system?|Explain source, treatment, storage, distribution, and monitoring at a high level.
rise_fall|A Lake's Decline or Recovery|Which measured changes explain one water body's trajectory?|Compare inflow, withdrawal, pollution, habitat, and restoration over time.
then_vs_now|One River Across Two Periods|How did flow, quality, ecology, and access change?|Use consistent sites, seasons, tests, and definitions.
future_developments|A Water Plan Under Climate Change|What would make a proposed supply plan resilient to uncertain conditions?|Compare demand, drought scenarios, source limits, cost, and equity.
myths_vs_facts|The Endless Groundwater Claim|Does recharge keep pace with withdrawals in one aquifer?|Compare dated levels, pumping estimates, recharge models, and uncertainty.
documentary_stories|A Drop's Local Journey|How does water move from catchment to use and back in one place?|Build a sourced timeline of physical flows and governing decisions.
observation_to_explanation|A Stream Turns Cloudy|Which evidence distinguishes erosion, discharge, and natural variation?|Collect upstream and downstream observations with timing and context.
measurement_method|Measuring a River|How do gauge placement and timing affect reported streamflow?|Compare methods, calibration, missing records, and uncertainty.
scale_and_timespan|A Wet Year Is Not a Trend|What period is needed to judge change in one water source?|Compare seasonal cycles, long records, and changes in measurement.
field_vs_lab|Water Sample Versus Watershed|Can one laboratory result represent a whole source?|Check sampling site, time, storage, detection limit, and spatial variation.
natural_variation|Why Water Quality Changes Daily|How much can a measured condition vary without a new pollution source?|Compare weather, flow, temperature, and repeated samples.
mechanism_chain|Land Use to River Flow|Which steps link one land change to a water outcome?|Test runoff, infiltration, erosion, and downstream measurements.
extreme_case|Water During a Drought|Which users and ecosystems lost access during a documented dry spell?|Compare supply, restrictions, demand, and recovery with dates.
classification_debate|When Is Water Scarce?|How do competing scarcity measures classify one region?|Compare quantity, timing, quality, accessibility, and environmental needs.
interacting_systems|Water, Energy, and Food|How did one water decision affect power and agriculture?|Trace withdrawals, return flows, timing, and tradeoffs.
data_gap|An Unmonitored Aquifer|Which missing wells or quality tests prevent a reliable assessment?|Map coverage, ownership, seasonal gaps, and uncertainty.
prediction_test|Did a Flood Forecast Help?|How did one forecast compare with observed levels and actions?|Check warning lead time, false alarms, reach, and outcomes.
human_impact|Who Pays for Water Changes?|How are shortages or quality problems distributed across residents?|Compare income, location, service continuity, and local testimony.
field_field_sampling|Taking a Representative Sample|Which collection choices affect one water-quality result?|Document site, depth, time, method, blanks, and chain of custody.
field_land_use|A Catchment After Development|How did land-cover change affect runoff and water quality?|Compare mapped change with matched rainfall and monitored flow.
field_weather_variability|Rainfall and River Response|How does the same river respond to different storm sequences?|Compare gauge records, antecedent moisture, and seasonal conditions.
field_habitat_change|Water for Wetland Life|How did flow or quality change affect one aquatic habitat?|Use species and hydrology measures with alternative explanations.
field_restoration_evidence|Did a River Repair Work?|What changed after one restoration project?|Compare preselected ecological, flood, and access outcomes with a baseline."""


FORESTS = """history_origins|How This Forest Formed|Which ecological and land-use history shaped one forest?|Use dated maps, disturbance records, species evidence, and local knowledge.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Forest in Context|What does one famous forest reveal and conceal about conservation?|Compare biodiversity, use rights, management, and neighboring landscapes.
hidden_stories|People in the Forest Record|Whose stewardship or labor is omitted from a forest's official history?|Use community-led accounts, tenure records, and consent.
beginner_explainers|What Is a Forest Ecosystem?|How do trees, soil, fungi, water, animals, and people interact in one place?|Use a bounded site and distinguish observations from models.
advanced_concepts|Forest Cover Versus Condition|Why can tree cover rise while ecological quality falls?|Compare native composition, age, connectivity, soil, and habitat use.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Did a Species Disappear Locally?|Which factors fit one documented decline?|Compare habitat, climate, disease, hunting, and survey coverage.
technology_innovation|Satellites and Forest Change|What can imagery reveal about one forest, and what can it miss?|Compare classification with ground plots and seasonal conditions.
people_personalities|Who Manages the Forest?|Which communities, agencies, and landowners shaped one management choice?|Trace authority, consent, livelihoods, and ecological evidence.
major_events|A Fire's Ecological Aftermath|How did one documented fire change habitat and recovery?|Compare burn severity, prior conditions, species response, and management.
how_it_works|From Seed to Canopy|Which processes govern regeneration in one forest type?|Follow seed supply, light, soil, herbivory, and disturbance evidence.
rise_fall|A Forest's Loss or Recovery|What explains a measured change in one forest area?|Compare land conversion, regrowth, definition, remote sensing, and tenure.
then_vs_now|One Forest Across Decades|How did structure, biodiversity, use, and governance change?|Use comparable plots and records with explicit method changes.
future_developments|A Forest Under Future Climate|Which uncertainties matter most for one management proposal?|Compare species ranges, drought, fire, land rights, and conditional scenarios.
myths_vs_facts|Planting Trees Equals Restoration?|Did one planting effort rebuild a functioning ecosystem?|Compare survival, species, soil, biodiversity, and local uses.
documentary_stories|A Forest Decision in Documents|How did one protected-area or harvest decision unfold?|Build dated record of evidence, consultation, rules, and observed effects.
observation_to_explanation|A Canopy Gap Appears|Which evidence distinguishes storm, logging, disease, and natural turnover?|Combine ground survey, imagery, and dated records.
measurement_method|Counting Forest Change|How do definitions and sensors change reported forest area?|Compare minimum cover, plantation treatment, resolution, and validation.
scale_and_timespan|Plot, Forest, Landscape|Can a short plot study support a regional forest claim?|Separate spatial scale, stand age, disturbance cycle, and sampling error.
field_vs_lab|Seedling Trial Meets Forest Floor|Do nursery results predict survival after planting?|Compare light, soil, water, competition, and monitoring duration.
natural_variation|Uneven Forest Growth|How much variation exists across slopes, soils, and years?|Use repeated plots and avoid treating one site as typical.
mechanism_chain|Fragmentation to Species Change|Which links connect habitat fragmentation to one species outcome?|Test movement, edge effects, reproduction, and alternative drivers.
extreme_case|Forest During a Severe Drought|Which species and functions changed during one extreme dry period?|Compare baseline, mortality, regeneration, and recovery.
classification_debate|What Counts as Forest?|How do ecological and administrative definitions differ for one landscape?|Compare canopy thresholds, plantations, community use, and implications.
interacting_systems|Forest and Water Together|How does one forest management change affect local water and soil?|Compare hydrology, erosion, climate, and scale with uncertainty.
data_gap|The Missing Forest Plot|Where is monitoring too sparse to support a biodiversity claim?|Map plot distribution, species detectability, and survey seasons.
prediction_test|Did a Fire-Risk Map Work?|How well did one prediction identify later fire impacts?|Compare forecast, observed burn pattern, exposure, and false alarms.
human_impact|Who Benefits From Protection?|How did one forest protection measure affect livelihoods and access?|Compare rights, compensation, ecological outcomes, and community accounts.
field_field_sampling|Surveying a Forest Plot|How do plot size and selection affect estimates of trees and species?|Document sampling frame, repeat visits, and identification uncertainty.
field_land_use|What Happened at the Edge?|How did neighboring land-use change affect forest condition?|Compare edge plots, land records, habitat, and alternative causes.
field_weather_variability|Weather Across a Forest|How do rainfall and heat vary across a forest's elevation or canopy?|Use local sensors and consistent periods with maintenance checks.
field_habitat_change|Tracking Habitat Quality|Which measured changes matter for one forest-dependent species?|Compare food, nesting, connectivity, and actual occupancy.
field_restoration_evidence|Did Forest Restoration Succeed?|What outcomes followed one reforestation or natural-regeneration project?|Compare survival, diversity, soil, water, and community goals against baseline."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("114", "114_water", WATER,
                  "Water as moving and governed systems of catchments, groundwater, quality, supply, ecosystems, and unequal access.",
                  "dated hydrologic and quality measurements, watershed and land-use maps, utility and allocation records, current health and environmental guidance, and attributed community accounts",
                  "Name source, catchment, jurisdiction, season, and test method. Do not infer potability from appearance or one sample; verify current local health and allocation guidance.")
    revise_domain("115", "115_forests_ecology", FORESTS,
                  "Forests as changing ecosystems shaped by species, disturbance, climate, land rights, stewardship, and human use.",
                  "dated field plots and species surveys, remote-sensing products with validation, land and management records, ecological studies, and consented local knowledge",
                  "Name forest type, site, tenure context, time span, and definition. Distinguish tree cover from ecological condition and respect Indigenous and local knowledge and land rights.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
